.TH "PB-ENV-LOAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-load - Load your workspace ENV into the current shell


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env load [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Load the ENV recorded by \fBpb env hook --install\fR into the current shell, like sourcing a file. This works only through the pb shell function the hook defines in new shells; without the hook this command only says how to set it up. Scripts and CI can use \fBpb env run -- <command>\fR instead.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for load


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb env hook --install   # once; then open a new shell
  pb env load
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
